  "Question": "What is the value of\n\n\\[\\frac{2}{10} + \\frac{4}{100} + \\frac{6}{1000}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.012\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.0246\\)",
    "C": "\\(0.12\\)",
    "D": "\\(0.246\\)",
    "E": "\\(246\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Since each denominator divides \\(1000\\), we can express every fraction in thousandths. This makes the fractional units the same size, so we can add their numerators:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{10}+\\frac{4}{100}+\\frac{6}{1000}\n&=\\frac{200}{1000}+\\frac{40}{1000}+\\frac{6}{1000}\\\\\n&=\\frac{246}{1000}=0.246.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe value is \\(0.246\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
